From: JiuJiuIos
Subject: [PATCH] ao_audiounit: set MaximumFramesPerSlice=4096 for lock screen

Apple QA1606 / WWDC: when the screen locks, RemoteIO may request up to
4096 frames per render callback. Default MaximumFramesPerSlice
(~1024/1156) causes kAudioUnitErr_TooManyFramesToProcess and audible
glitches. AVPlayer handles this internally; stock mpv ao_audiounit does not.

Apply after AudioUnitInitialize, before AudioOutputUnitStart.
Stack after media-kit's mpv-audiounit-skip-session-management.patch.

App currently mitigates via Bridge/AudioUnitLockScreenFix.m (fishhook).
Prefer baking this into a rebuilt Mpv.xcframework and removing the hook.

--- a/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m
+++ b/audio/out/ao_audiounit.m
@@ -148,6 +148,16 @@ static bool init_audiounit(struct ao *ao)
     err = AudioUnitInitialize(p->audio_unit);
     CHECK_CA_ERROR_L(coreaudio_error_component,
                      "unable to initialize audio unit");
 
+    // Lock screen enlarges IO slices to ~4096 frames @ 44.1kHz.
+    UInt32 max_frames = 4096;
+    err = AudioUnitSetProperty(p->audio_unit,
+                               kAudioUnitProperty_MaximumFramesPerSlice,
+                               kAudioUnitScope_Global, 0,
+                               &max_frames, sizeof(max_frames));
+    CHECK_CA_ERROR_L(coreaudio_error_audiounit,
+                     "unable to set MaximumFramesPerSlice");
+
     err = au_get_ary(p->audio_unit, kAudioUnitProperty_AudioChannelLayout, kAudioUnitScope_Output,
                      0, (void**)&layout, &size);
     CHECK_CA_ERROR_L(coreaudio_error_audiounit,
